---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Commands from '../components/Commands.astro';
import FlowFigure from '../components/FlowFigure.astro';
import Mark from '../components/Mark.astro';
import Typed from '../components/Typed.astro';
import { commands, links, site } from '../config';

const nodes = [
  ['Start', 'Begins a run by hand.'],
  ['Webhook', 'Begins a run from an incoming request.'],
  ['HTTP Request', 'Calls an outside service, with separate paths for success and error.'],
  ['Condition', 'Sends the run down a true or a false path.'],
  ['Evaluate Code', 'Runs Elixir or Python with access to the flow’s context.'],
  ['Variable', 'Keeps a typed value for later nodes.'],
  ['Logger', 'Writes a message to the application logs.'],
  ['Output', 'Ends the run and returns the final context.'],
];

const leader = 16;
---

<Base>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

  <svg class="sr-only" aria-hidden="true">
    <filter id="struck">
      <feTurbulence type="fractalNoise" baseFrequency="0.7" numOctaves="2" seed="3" />
      <feDisplacementMap in="SourceGraphic" scale="0.9" />
    </filter>
  </svg>

  <header class="sheet masthead">
    <a class="brand" href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL} aria-label={`${site.name}, home`}>
      <Mark />
      <span>{site.name}</span>
    </a>
    <nav aria-label="Main">
      <a href="#how-it-runs">How it runs</a>
      <a href="#start">Get started</a>
      <a href={links.source}>GitHub</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="main" class="sheet">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1><Typed lines={['Every thread goes', 'where it should.']} accent="thread" /></h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Heddle is an open-source workflow engine. Draw your business logic as a flow of nodes,
        and it runs on Elixir, one step at a time, with a record of what happened.
      </p>
      <p class="actions">
        <a href={links.install}>[ Read the install guide ]</a>
        <a href={links.source}>[ Source on GitHub ]</a>
      </p>
      <p class="entry">
        <strong>heddle</strong> <span class="ipa">/ˈhɛd.əl/</span> <em>noun.</em> The part of a loom
        that lifts each warp thread so the weft can pass through. It decides which way every thread
        goes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="break" aria-hidden="true">* * *</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="flow">
      <h2 id="flow" data-n="1.">A flow, drawn</h2>
      <p>
        A webhook comes in. A condition checks it. One path calls another service, the other writes
        a line to the log, and both finish in the same place. Each step is a node, and each run
        follows one thread through them.
      </p>
      <FlowFigure />
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="parts">
      <h2 id="parts" data-n="2.">The parts</h2>
      <p>Heddle ships with eight nodes.</p>
      <dl class="parts">
        {
          nodes.map(([name, text]) => (
            <div>
              <dt>
                {name}
                <span class="dots" aria-hidden="true">
                  {' '}
                  {'.'.repeat(leader - (name?.length ?? 0))}
                </span>
              </dt>
              <dd>{text}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
      <p>
        Rather not start from a blank page? Describe the flow in the AI chat. It proposes a plan,
        and builds the flow once you approve it. This part needs an OpenAI key. Other systems can
        reach the same flows through the <a href={links.api}>public API</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="how-it-runs">
      <h2 id="how-it-runs" data-n="3.">How it runs</h2>
      <p>
        Two roles share one Postgres database. The UI serves the editor, takes requests and puts each
        run in a queue. Workers take runs from the queue and execute them. A run that fails gets up
        to three attempts.
      </p>
      <p>When the queue grows, add workers:</p>
      <Commands lines={commands.scale} />
      <p>The <a href={links.scaling}>scaling guide</a> covers the rest.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="start">
      <h2 id="start" data-n="4.">Start it on your machine</h2>
      <p>You need Git and Docker.</p>
      <Commands lines={commands.start} />
      <p>
        Then open <code>localhost:4000</code>. To run from source instead, follow the
        <a href={links.install}>install guide</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="open">
      <h2 id="open" data-n="5.">In the open</h2>
      <p>
        Heddle is MIT licensed and built in public. The plans are on the
        <a href={links.roadmap}>roadmap</a>, the work in progress is on the
        <a href={links.board}>project board</a>, and the conversation is on
        <a href={links.discord}>Discord</a>. If you want to help, start with the
        <a href={links.contributing}>contributing guide</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="sheet colophon">
    <p>
      {site.name}
      {site.version}. <a href={links.license}>MIT license</a>.
    </p>
    <p>Set in Courier Prime and iA Writer Quattro.</p>
    <p class="folio" aria-hidden="true">- 1 -</p>
  </footer>
</Base>

<style>
  .masthead {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
    padding-block: var(--space-4) 0;
    font-family: var(--font-type);
  }

  .brand {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0 var(--space-3);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  nav a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
  }

  .hero {
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 14vh, 8rem) var(--space-5);
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-type);
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, calc(9.4vw - 4px), 3.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    filter: url('#struck');
  }

  .lead {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-4);
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-1) var(--space-4);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-4);
    font-family: var(--font-type);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .actions a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .entry {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-5);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .entry strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font-type);
  }

  .ipa {
    font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
  }

  .break {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-type);
    text-align: center;
  }

  section + section,
  .break + section {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-6);
  }

  h2 {
    position: relative;
    margin-block-end: var(--space-3);
    font-family: var(--font-type);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-underline-offset: 0.3em;
    scroll-margin-block-start: var(--space-4);
  }

  h2::before {
    content: attr(data-n) ' ';
    color: var(--ribbon);
    white-space: pre;
  }

  section p + p {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  .parts {
    margin-block: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
  }

  .parts div {
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
  }

  dt {
    font-family: var(--font-type);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .dots {
    display: none;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  code {
    font-family: var(--font-type);
  }

  .colophon {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-6);
    padding-block-end: var(--space-4);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .folio {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-4);
    font-family: var(--font-type);
    text-align: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .parts div {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 17ch 1fr;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: var(--space-3);
      padding-block: var(--space-1);
    }

    dt {
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: inherit;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .dots {
      display: inline;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    h2::before {
      position: absolute;
      inset-inline-end: 100%;
      margin-inline-end: var(--space-3);
    }
  }
</style>
